<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">drain</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">drain</ansi> command is the vampire's signature lifesteal move.
It strikes the target with raking <ansi fg="item">claws</ansi>, sapping their
vitality and channeling it back into the vampire. A
successful hit also leaves the target bleeding.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must have the LifeDrain species flag (vampire only)
  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">drain</ansi>
  Attempt to drain your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Moderate — lighter than a full melee strike; the
    lifesteal makes up the difference in sustained fights.
  <ansi fg="stat">Lifesteal:</ansi> On a hit, the attacker heals for a fraction of
    damage dealt (governed by the DrainHealRatio balance knob,
    default 75%).
  <ansi fg="stat">Bleed:</ansi> The target gains a Bleeding condition on hit,
    dealing ongoing damage each round.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with other special moves.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Drain is most effective when the vampire is wounded — the
combined bleed and heal make it excellent for sustained
pressure. Unlike most beast moves, drain is not gated on
a natural attack type; it is gated on the LifeDrain species
flag, making it the vampire's exclusive ability.

